# Keep the build context to what the image needs.
*
!cms/
!content/
!rebuild/
!dist/
!build-from-content.mjs
!build-static.mjs
!build-store.mjs

# This list is an allowlist: anything not named here is invisible to the build.
# A COPY of a file missing from it fails with "not found" even though the file
# is committed, which is exactly how build-store.mjs broke the image.

# ...with three exceptions carved back out, because !content/ would otherwise
# sweep in everything underneath it. Later rules win.
#
# content/products/ is the files customers pay for. They belong in the volume on
# the server, put there by hand, and must never be baked into an image that
# could be pushed to a registry.
content/products/
# Runtime state. Orders hold customer emails; analytics holds per-day visitor
# hashes. Both are written by the running site and live in the volume.
content/orders/
content/analytics/
